### ✅ Verified Clean
- `src/engine/resolve-review-loop.js:98` — `assertOneOf(value, 'reviewer_runner', [...])` enum extended to include `'anthropic-compatible'`. Verified this closes a **real, live parity gap**: `scripts/resolve-review-loop.sh:257` already accepts `anthropic-compatible` as a valid `reviewer_runner` (pre-existing code, not touched by this diff), and `hooks/tests/resolve-review-loop.test.sh:87-89` already asserts the shell side honors it — but the JS-side validator's enum was one entry short of the shell's, and this validator is consumed in production by `src/engine/autopilot-engine.js:9,795` (`resolveReviewLoopJson`) via `bin/autopilot.js`. Before this fix, any project with `reviewer_runner: anthropic-compatible` configured would pass shell resolution but throw inside the JS engine layer (`must be one of: codex, auto, agy, grok, cc-shim`). Genuine bug fix, correctly scoped.
