- `hooks/tests/contract-parity.test.sh` new Case C (lines 138-173) — traced the full assertion chain: (1) shell resolve exits 0 and preserves `reviewer_runner: anthropic-compatible` (line 144-150); (2) stderr contains no "error"/"block" — verified by reading `scripts/resolve-review-loop.sh` end-to-end that no diagnostic branch fires for this minimal 2-key config (cross-family check is satisfied by default `qc_panel`/`implementer_engine`, endpoint/`on_engine_unavailable` warnings don't fire since those keys are unset, and the `engine-capability-state.js` subprocess output is JSON-captured via stdout, never leaked to this script's own stderr); (3) the JS module (`resolveReviewLoopJson`) resolves the same runner value without error, confirming shell/JS parity is the actual thing under test; (4) `validate-parity.js` accepts the output. Test is non-redundant with `resolve-review-loop.test.sh` (which only checks shell `--field` output, never the JS-side `validateReviewLoopConfig`).
